  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2.3. Increased capacity of Member States to engage in a forward-looking international labour standards policy</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Existing national tripartite dialogue was strengthened to discuss ILS-related matters. A Consultation  on the reports to the CEACR was conducted for the first time in Nepal  in August 2023. ILO organized tripartite workshops in March 2022 and March 2023, to strengthen the capacity of the tripartite partners to prepare informative reports to the CEACR, responding to the comments of the supervisory bodies, and helped to develop work plan which included tripartite consultation on the draft reports.

Five representatives from Nepal (tripartite) participated in the ITC International Labour Standards Academy (Asia and the Pacific) in May 2022.</narrative>
   </description>
