   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2.3. Increased capacity of Member States to engage in a forward-looking international labour standards policy</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Ministry of Labour, Employment, and Social Security (MoLESS) submitted reports due in 2022 (C029, C105, C138, and C182) before September 1, 2022, and provided replies to the comments of the ILO supervisory bodies. The MoLESS submitted  reports due for  2023 on C100, C111, C169, and C182 in 2023, responding to the comments of the ILO supervisory bodies before September 1, 2023. The ILO organized tripartite workshop in March 2023 to strengthen the capacity of constituents to prepare informative reports to the CEACR, responding to the comments of the supervisory bodies. In 2023 the ILO prepared a Normative Stocktaking Report (NSR) which served the basis for discussion on normative priorities of Nepal. 

The ILO held a training for the government on reporting to the CEACR, focused on C182 on 15 August 2023

Five representatives from Nepal participated the ITC International Labour Standards Academy (Asia and the Pacific) in May 2022.</narrative>
   </description>
